# Deployment facts

Application versions overlap for up to twenty minutes during rollout; rollback to the prior image remains available for one hour.
The proposed child table uses policy_id plus ordinal as its primary key and stores the complete rule JSON, so duplicate actions and unknown keys can remain distinct.
Backfill can run in batches and can be retried using the same policy_id and ordinal key.
Policy edits continue while backfill runs; no write lock is planned.
The existing payload column can remain while both old and new application versions are deployed.
No other service or third-party database is planned.
Dropping payload would prevent the old image and hourly exporter from reading policies.
